    "result_text": "The full suite is green (the only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, both tests pass, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` derived field: **SILVER** when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise **BRONZE**.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the other derived fields like `membershipNumber`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\", expression = \"java(membershipTier(owner))\")` plus a small `membershipTier(Owner)` default method that returns `\"SILVER\"` when `namesakeCount == 0` and email is non-empty, else `\"BRONZE\"`.\n\nThis keeps the tier logic co-located with the other derived-field logic in the mapper (single responsibility, reusing the existing derivation pattern) rather than adding it to the `Owner` entity or a controller. Both new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) and the full suite pass.",
